# Repo-level files. These live in the dotfiles repo but must never be
# installed into $HOME.
#
# Patterns match with doublestar against the TARGET path and are anchored at
# the destination root -- this is NOT gitignore semantics. So `README.md` here
# means ~/README.md only; it does not affect ~/.config/nvim/docs/keymaps.md.
#
# Source entries beginning with "." (.github/, .gitignore) are ignored by
# chezmoi automatically and need no entry here.
README.md
CLAUDE.md
Brewfile
LICENSE

# Generated or private files inside directories we DO manage. chezmoi only
# tracks what is explicitly added, but these are listed so an accidental
# `chezmoi add ~/.config/zsh-ghostty` cannot sweep them in.
.config/zsh-ghostty/.zsh_history
.config/zsh-ghostty/.zcompdump*
.config/zsh-ghostty/*.bak

# Same idea for the pi coding agent (~/.pi/agent/): auth.json holds the Z.ai
# API key and is a SECRET, models-store.json is a catalog cache pi refetches
# from the provider, and sessions/ is transcripts. An accidental
# `chezmoi add ~/.pi` must not sweep any of them into the repo.
.pi/agent/auth.json
.pi/agent/models-store.json
.pi/agent/sessions
